    <help format="markdown"><![CDATA[
**DNAapler** moves the start of a circular microbial sequence to a marker gene or
predicted coding sequence. FASTA does not record circularity; rotating a linear
sequence joins its ends.

**Methods.** All searches bundled DnaA, COG1474, RepA, and TerL markers for each
record. When families compete, that order takes precedence over hit score. All
cannot use a custom database. Use Custom for one sequence or Bulk with Custom
for multiple records in one dataset.

**GFA and outputs.** Only simple circular GFA segments are reoriented; linear
segments pass through. The FASTA output contains every GFA segment. All keeps
searched records without marker hits in its FASTA and summary. Bulk puts
unmatched records in a separate collection; for GFA input, they also remain in
the main FASTA. In mixed GFA, summaries cover only processed circular segments.
A GFA with no circular segments passes through with summary rows for all
segments; a Bulk search of eligible segments with no hits fails.
    ]]></help>
    <expand macro="citations"/>
</tool>
